(10. Security and Engineering Notes) Tj
0 -14 Td
(10.1 Current strengths) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Route-level auth and role checks are present.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- HttpOnly cookie is used.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Passwords are hashed with SHA-256 before storage \(for new updates\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Asset path resolution has traversal protection.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(10.2 Current limitations / improvements suggested) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Sessions are in-memory only \(lost on restart; not multi-instance safe\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- No CSRF protection for form endpoints yet.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Password hashing is plain SHA-256 without salt/stretching.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  Recommended: bcrypt/argon2.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- DB password default is hardcoded fallback in code; should rely fully on env vars.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Multipart parsing is handcrafted; using a robust parser/framework would reduce risk.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- No explicit rate-limiting for login/contact routes.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(11. End-to-End Request Lifecycle \(Example\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Example: user registers for an event) Tj
0 -14 Td
(1. User opens browse page and clicks Register.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. Frontend opens modal, submits form data to /register-event.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. Backend validates session + required fields + consent + event id.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. Backend UPSERTs user_event_registrations row.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(5. Backend returns JSON success with ticket info.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(6. Frontend updates card state, reloads tickets/bookings/dashboard widgets.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(7. Subsequent pages fetch fresh data from tickets/bookings endpoints.) Tj
ET
